script:
export const meta = {
  name: "fala-multiuser-foundation",
  description: "Phase 1 of FALA voice web app: per-user persistence + multi-session engines (contract terms 1, 2, 8)",
  phases: [
    { title: "implement" },
    { title: "verify" },
    { title: "repair" },
  ],
};

const PROJECT = "/home/alex/Projects/FALA";

const CONTEXT = `
Project: ${PROJECT} — FALA, a European Portuguese CLI tutor (Python 3.10+).
Key files: config.py (module-level path constants: DATA_DIR, SUMMARY_PATH, VOCABULARY_PATH, SESSIONS_DIR, RECORDS_DIR),
progress.py (imports those constants; functions load_summary/save_summary/load_vocabulary/save_vocabulary/get_review_words/update_vocab_after_review/add_vocabulary/save_learning_record/get_vocab_for_prompt/vocabulary_report),
conversation.py (ConversationEngine — calls progress functions, owns session lifecycle),
web.py (FastAPI prototype: single GLOBAL engine + module-level _session_started/_session_ended booleans — this is what we are replacing),
fala.py (CLI entrypoint — must keep working unchanged from a user's perspective).
Tests: run with: cd ${PROJECT} && .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q   (77 currently green)
Lint/type: cd ${PROJECT} && scripts/lint.sh   (ruff + ruff format + mypy — must stay clean)
Python 3.10 syntax. Do NOT modify audio.py or prompts/. Do NOT weaken existing tests.
`;

const DESIGN = `
Design decisions (already made — implement these, don't re-litigate):
1. Per-user data layout: data/users/<user_id>/{summary.md, vocabulary.md, sessions/, records/} for non-default users.
2. The special user id "default" maps to the EXISTING flat data/ paths (no file migration, zero risk to current CLI behavior). This is how the existing single-user data "becomes the default user".
3. config.py gains a paths resolver, e.g. paths_for_user(user_id: str) -> dict or small dataclass with summary/vocabulary/sessions/records/data-dir entries, creating dirs as needed. Existing module-level constants stay for backward compat.
4. progress.py functions gain an optional paths parameter (default = current behavior). Thread paths through rather than reading config globals at call time.
5. ConversationEngine.__init__ gains user_id: str = "default" (or a paths object) and passes resolved paths to every progress call. CLI (fala.py) keeps using the default user.
6. web.py: replace global engine + booleans with a session store: dict[str, SessionState] keyed by a "fala_session" cookie (uuid4, httponly, set on first request if absent). SessionState holds user_id, engine (ConversationEngine | None), session_started/ended flags, last_active. For now user_id == the session id (invite-code auth in a later phase will bind real user ids). /start creates an engine for that user; /quit and "quit"/"exit"/"sair" in /message end it and clear the engine so a new /start works. Concurrent users must never share an engine.
7. No idle-session reaper needed yet — leave a TODO comment.
`;

phase("implement");

const impl = await agent(`${CONTEXT}\n${DESIGN}
Task: implement items 1-5 (config paths resolver, progress.py paths threading, ConversationEngine user_id). Keep CLI behavior byte-identical for the default user. Add focused tests: paths resolver (default vs named user), per-user vocab isolation through ConversationEngine (mock LLM calls as existing tests do — check tests/conftest.py for the established pattern). Run the full test suite and scripts/lint.sh; iterate until 100% green. Return a concise summary: files changed, tests added, final pytest/lint status.`, { label: "foundation-impl" });
if (impl === null) throw new Error("foundation-impl agent failed");
log("foundation-impl done");

const webImpl = await agent(`${CONTEXT}\n${DESIGN}
The foundation (items 1-5) was just implemented by a prior agent with this summary:
---
${impl}
---
Task: implement item 6 — rewrite web.py's session handling to the cookie-keyed session store. Keep the existing endpoints and HTML page contract intact (tests/test_web.py must keep passing; update it only where the old global-state assumptions were being tested, and extend it: new tests proving two distinct cookies get isolated engines and isolated vocabularies, and that /quit then /start works on the same cookie). Run the full test suite and scripts/lint.sh; iterate until 100% green. Return a concise summary: files changed, tests added/changed, final pytest/lint status.`, { label: "web-sessions-impl" });
if (webImpl === null) throw new Error("web-sessions-impl agent failed");
log("web-sessions-impl done");

phase("verify");

const verdict = await agent(`${CONTEXT}\n${DESIGN}
Two agents just implemented the multi-user foundation. Their summaries:
--- foundation-impl ---
${impl}
--- web-sessions-impl ---
${webImpl}
---
Independently VERIFY, do not trust the summaries. Check each contract term:
T1 multi-user isolation: read web.py + conversation.py; confirm no module-level engine state remains; confirm two cookie sessions cannot share an engine or vocabulary.
T2 per-user persistence: confirm paths_for_user("default") resolves to the existing flat data/ paths and any other id resolves under data/users/<id>/ with dirs auto-created; confirm no progress.py function still reads config path globals directly at call time.
T8 quality gates: run: cd ${PROJECT} && .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q   and   scripts/lint.sh   — both must pass; note exact failure output if not.
Also sanity-check: fala.py untouched in behavior; no new dependencies added without necessity; SessionState cleanup TODO present.
Return JSON: {"pass": boolean, "issues": [strings describing concrete problems, empty if none], "tests_green": boolean, "lint_clean": boolean}`, {
  label: "foundation-review",
  schema: {
    type: "object",
    properties: {
      pass: { type: "boolean" },
      issues: { type: "array", items: { type: "string" } },
      tests_green: { type: "boolean" },
      lint_clean: { type: "boolean" },
    },
    required: ["pass", "issues", "tests_green", "lint_clean"],
    additionalProperties: false,
  },
});
if (verdict === null) throw new Error("foundation-review agent failed");
log(`review: pass=${verdict.pass} tests=${verdict.tests_green} lint=${verdict.lint_clean} issues=${verdict.issues.length}`);

phase("repair");

let repair = null;
if (!verdict.pass) {
  repair = await agent(`${CONTEXT}\n${DESIGN}
The verification pass on the multi-user foundation FAILED with these concrete issues:
${verdict.issues.map((i, n) => `${n + 1}. ${i}`).join("\n")}
Fix every listed issue in the repo at ${PROJECT}. Re-run the full test suite and scripts/lint.sh until green. Do not redesign — minimal targeted fixes. Return a concise summary of what you changed and final test/lint status.`, { label: "foundation-repair" });
  if (repair === null) log("repair agent returned no result — issues may remain");
} else {
  log("verification passed — no repair needed");
}

return {
  contract_terms: ["T1 multi-user sessions", "T2 per-user persistence", "T8 quality gates"],
  verified: verdict.pass,
  issues_found: verdict.issues,
  implementation: impl,
  web_layer: webImpl,
  repair,
};
